.TH HMAP_DUMP 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
hmap_dump \- Dump the contents of a hash map to a buffer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/hmap.h>

.IB void
.IB hmap_dump(HMAP_DB* hmap, buffer* b);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBhmap_dump\fR function dumps the contents of a hash map to a buffer. It takes a pointer to the hash map database and a pointer to the buffer as arguments.

The function takes the following parameters:
.IB HMAP_DB*
A pointer to the hash map database.
.IB buffer*
A pointer to the buffer where the contents of the hash map will be dumped.

The function does not return any value. It populates the buffer with the contents of the hash map in a specific format.

The \fBhmap_dump\fR function is intended to be used to dump the contents of a hash map to a buffer for debugging or logging purposes.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBhmap_dump\fR function to dump the contents of a hash map to a buffer:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/hmap.h>
#include <lib/buffer.h>

int main() {
    HMAP_DB* hmap_db;
    // Initialize the hash map database
    hmap_init(&hmap_db);

    // Add tuples to the hash map
    hmap_add_tuple_with_data(&hmap_db, "example1", 8, "data1");
    hmap_add_tuple_with_data(&hmap_db, "example2", 8, "data2");

    // Create a buffer to hold the dump
    buffer* b = buffer_new();

    // Dump the contents of the hash map to the buffer
    hmap_dump(hmap_db, b);

    // Print the contents of the buffer
    printf("Dump of hash map:\n%s\n", buffer_data(b));

    // Free the hash map database and buffer
    hmap_destroy(&hmap_db);
    buffer_free(b);

    return 0;
}
.nef